[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known: one bug, one fix queued. Its reports describe three
problems. Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October with an answer for two of them. The third is
still open.

<Callout kind="warn">
The <code>one-day</code> reports are not covered by the parser fix or by retiring booking-v3.
Keep them out of any "fixed" reply, and route new one-day reports to its ticket, not to #4471.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  tickets={{
    parser: { url: 'https://github.com/jbandi/mega-s01e03-support-kb/issues/1', state: 'closed · fixed' },
    hint: { url: 'https://github.com/jbandi/mega-s01e03-support-kb/issues/2', state: "closed · won't fix" },
    'one-day': { url: 'https://github.com/jbandi/mega-s01e03-support-kb/issues/3', state: 'open' },
  }}
/>

## What engineering did

- **`parser` — fixed.** `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. Reports from day-first tenants
  through app, email and `DD/MM/YYYY` forms should stop.
- **`hint` — won't fix.** The booking-v3 form is retired, so its `MM/DD/YYYY` hint goes with it.
  Tenants still on booking-v3 need to move off it.
- **`one-day` — nothing yet.** The booking lands one day early: "Invite says Tuesday 12 May.
  Calendar says Monday 11 May" (R-41202), "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got
  Monday" (R-41344), "The invite arrived before I made the booking" (R-41236). A day/month flip
  cannot do that, so the parser fix does not close it. The latest came in on 4 October (R-41620).

## How each report was placed

1. **One report per id.** The export repeats some reports across its pages; each id counts once.
2. **`hint`** — a day-first tenant on `booking-v3`, reporting through the form. That form prints
   `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, people type month first as told, and the form reads it the
   tenant's way.
3. **`parser`** — every other report from a day-first tenant. This is the desk's own count
   (`causes.ts`), the same as the table on #4471.
4. **`one-day`** — the reports the desk itself lists in `desk-notes.json` as a one-day move. The
   desk counts them under `parser`, where they are filed; they are also a problem of their own.

The intake tag (`meta.intakeTag`) is not used. It is guessed from the reporter's browser and often
disagrees with the tenant's locale and form (see the tag column on [#4471](/kb/incidents/4471)).

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone. All three
problems produce the same subjects ("Wrong day on the invite", "Date is wrong"), so all three
landed in #4471 and inherited its "known" status, and then its close.

